      "writtenOn": "2021-02-22T17:50:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "They don\u0027t exist here because they don\u0027t have well defined times that they start, like the _entry of the state, and do not have well defined times they stop, like the _exit of the state. The examples you mentioned have helper routines that are called from different states and the need for the timer stops at some other location. If the path is interrupted then the timer would remain active. I chose to limit the PD Timers to just those that had a clear _entry, usage, _exit pattern.  It does not mean these exceptions could not be adjusted to work in this framework but they would be highly susceptible to errors and I didn\u0027t find the risk worth taking.",
